<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Texas harvest progresses.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Texas harvest progresses.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harvesting of hard red winter wheat in northern Texas was finally progressing Tuersday after a two-week delay, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The harvest is starting to kick up down in Fort Worth. What we're seeing is mostly number one grade wheat,&quot; a south central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The wheat that's coming off looks to be of good quality. The test weights are high,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, more rain fell Tuesday morning in western Kansas, and merchandisers said growers were beginning to wish for a return to drier conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;There's been more rain in western Kansas today and there's a chance for (rain) to fall in the central part of the state,&quot; a south central Kansas dealer said. &quot;(Farmers) would just as soon have some warmth now, but nobody's complaining too hard.&quot;  </p>
